  "body": "Before #7166, there was no way to observe whether a `setTimeout()` timer's ID is in the list of active timers after the timer callback has been run, and so the timer task does not remove that ID from the list. However, that PR made the list of active timers into a map of active timers that is used to determine the idle deadline to use for the `requestIdleCallback()` API, and such timer ID's would result in the computed deadline being in the past if any `setTimeout()` timer was started and its callback was run.",
